last_n_rolling_months / last_n_years with {n}, this_calendar_month / this_calendar_quarter /
this_calendar_year (year-to-date) / this_week, previous_calendar_month / previous_calendar_quarter /
previous_calendar_year, calendar_year {year}, calendar_quarter {year,quarter}, calendar_month_range {year,monthStart,monthEnd}.
Ranges are half-open [start, endExclusive). The backend resolves relative kinds using the business timezone.
Legacy relativeDateToken values still work but are limited; prefer dateRangeJson for arbitrary N and historical periods.
Do not claim only a fixed token list is supported. If the user says "six months within 2025" without which months, ask which period.

Aggregations (operation=aggregate): pass aggregatesJson=[{function,field,alias}] and optional groupByJson=[{field,alias,dateGrouping?}].
